X:33
T:Fine Flowers in the Valley
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:Em
%
"Am" A2 AG E2 E2 | A2 AG "Em" E4 | "Am"  c4 "G" BB cd | d4 "Am" c2 cd |
w: 1.~She sat_ down be-low a_ thorn, Fine flow-ers in the val-ley, An' _
"C" e2 e2 "G" d2 cB | "Am" AB c2 "Em" E2 EE | "Am" E2 c2 "G" cB AG | "Am" A4 A4 |]
w: there she has her_ sweet_ babe born, And the green leaves they_ grow_ rar-ely.
%
%
W: 2. "Smile na sae sweet, my bonnie babe,"
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: "An ye'll smile sae sweet, ye'll smile me deid."
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
W:
W: 3. She's ta'en oot her wee pen knife
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: And twinned the sweet babe o' it's life.
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
W:
W: 4. She's howket a grave by the light o' the moon,
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: An' there she's buried her sweet babe in.
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
W:
W: 5. As she was going to the church,
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: She saw a sweet babe in the porch
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
W:
W: 6. "O sweet babe, an' thou were mine,"
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: "I wad cleed thee in the silk sae fine."
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
W:
W: 7. "O mither dear, when I was thine,"
W: Fine flowers in the valley,
W: "Ye didna prove tae me sae kind."
W: And the green leaves they grow rarely.
%
