K:Dmix
%
z4 z2 Ad A3 G | F2 DD D E2 F | "C" G2 E2 C2 AF GB "D" A3 G | "C" E2 D2 "D" D2 "^Chorus:" F>G ||
w: gie my pipes an-o-ther blaw, and I'll gang_ o'er the hills to Gal-lo-wa'. Oh the
%
A>A d2 F3 G | AF GB "D" A3 G | "C" E2 D2 "D" D4 |]
w: hea-ther bells and ri-vers all, an I'll go oot oer the hills to Gal-lo-wa'.
%
%
%%leftmargin 2.0in
%%rightmargin 2.0in
%
W: 1. I'll take my plaidie contented to be,
W: A wee bit kilted above my knee,
W: And I'll gie my pipes another blaw,
W: And I'll gang o'er the hills to Gallowa'.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Oh the Gallowa' hills are covered with broom,
W: With heather bells in bonnie bloom.
W: With heather bells and rivers all,
W: An I'll go oot oer the hills to Gallowa'.
W:
W: 2. And it's hey Bonnie Lass will you come with me,
W: And share my lot in a strange country?
W: And will you take the long road over the fells,
W: And go over the hills to Gallowa'?
W: [Chorus:]
W:
W: 3. I'll sell my rod, I sell my reel,
W: I'll sell my only spinning wheel.
W: Then I'll take the long road over the fells,
W: And go over the hills to Gallowa'.
W: [Chorus:]
