X:69
T:Will Ye Go Lassie Go
T:Wild Mountain Thyme
C:Trad
O:Scotland
F:http://folk-lyrics.co.uk/Songs/WillYeGoLassieGo
M:C
L:1/8
K:D
%
DE|"D"FF3 "A"E3D|"D"B,D3 z2 FA|"G"B3B "Em" B3A|
w: Oh, the summ-er-time is com-ing And the trees are sweet-ly
"D"FA3 z2 FA|"G"B4 "F#m"A2F2|"Bm"ED3 z2 EF|"C"G3F "Em" E2D2|
w: bloom-in', And the wild moun-tain thyme* Grows a-round the pur-ple
"G"B,D3 D3B,|"D" A,4 "G"B,D3|"D"D4 z2 FA|
w: heath-er; Will ye go, las-sie, go? And we'll
"G"B4 B3A|"D"FA3 z2 FA|"G"B4 "F#m"A2F2|"Bm"ED3 z2 EF|
w: all go to-geth-er, To pull wild moun-tain thyme* All a-
"Em"G3F "C" E2D2|"G"B,D3 D2B,2|"D" A,4 "G"B,D3|"D"D6|]
w: round the pur-ple heath-er; Will ye go, las-sie, go?
%
%
W:1. Oh, the summertime is coming
W:And the trees are sweetly bloomin',
W:And the wild mountain thyme
W:Grows around the purple heather;
W:Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:
W:(Chorus:)
W:  And we'll all go together,
W:  To pull wild mountain thyme
W:  All around the purple heather;
W:  Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:
W:2. I will build my love a tower
W:By yon pure, crystal fountain,
W:And it's there I will bring
W:All the flowers of the mountain;
W:Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:3. I will range through the wilds
W:And the deep land so dreary
W:And return with the spoils
W:To the bower o' my dearie;
W:Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:4. If my true love will not come
W:I will surely find another
W:To pull wild mountain thyme
W:All around the purple heather;
W:Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:(Chorus:)
W:
W:5. Oh, the autumn-time is comin'
W:And the leaves will soon be fallin',
W:And the blossoms o' the summer
W:Will soon wither on the mountain;
W:Will ye go, lassie, go?
W:(Chorus:)
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_ab4f0534.abc

